            <ArticleTitle>Rethinking animal models and human obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>384-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1152/physiol.00043.2014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Human obesity is a complex phenomenon where economic, cultural, behavioral, and biological factors intersect in the physiological space. Developing animal models that capture several elements of the many potential interactions between these factors will only increase their translational value.</AbstractText>
